devices=2
affected = the hostcall kernel is REFUSED, or its marker never prints,
           while the plain kernel is ok on the same device

--- device 0 (gfx1100) ---
  plain     ok        launch:no error | sync:no error | lastError:no error
    [device] HOSTCALL_MARKER reached the host
  hostcall  ok        launch:no error | sync:no error | lastError:no error

--- device 1 (gfx1100) ---
  plain     ok        launch:no error | sync:no error | lastError:no error
    [device] HOSTCALL_MARKER reached the host
  hostcall  ok        launch:no error | sync:no error | lastError:no error

If no '[device] HOSTCALL_MARKER' line appeared for a device, hostcall is
unavailable there, whatever the return codes said.
